# Resume JSON from PDF

The Career page (`/career`) loads data dynamically from locale files:
- **`public/resume/resume.ru.json`**
- **`public/resume/resume.en.json`**

Keep **`public/resume/resume.json`** in sync with `resume.ru.json` when updating.

Do not store resume content in `src/data/`. The hh.ru/rabota.by PDF is the source of truth for static export; JSON drives the web page and generated PDF.

## Files

| File | Role |
|------|------|
| `public/resume/FM-resume.pdf` | Static CV (rabota.by download button) |
| `public/resume/avatar.jpg` | Photo for generated PDF (`personal.photoUrl`) |
| `public/resume/resume.ru.json` | Resume data (Russian) |
| `public/resume/resume.en.json` | Resume data (English) |
| `public/resume/resume.json` | Legacy copy — sync with RU |
| `src/i18n/en.ts`, `src/i18n/ru.ts` | Career UI translations (not resume body text) |
| `src/types/resume.ts` | Schema including `photoUrl`, `pdfUrl` |
| `src/utils/generateResumePdf.ts` | Generated PDF builder |
| `.cursor/rules/career-cv-pdf.mdc` | PDF generator rules |

## When to regenerate JSON

Regenerate locale JSON when:
- `FM-resume.pdf` is replaced or updated
- User asks to sync career data from PDF

## Workflow

1. Read `public/resume/FM-resume.pdf` fully
2. Map PDF sections → JSON fields (see mapping below)
3. Write/update **`public/resume/resume.ru.json`** and **`public/resume/resume.en.json`**
4. Sync **`public/resume/resume.json`** with RU version if it exists
5. Set `meta.updatedAt` from PDF footer ("Резюме обновлено …")
6. Increment `meta.version` if structure changed
7. Run `pnpm build` to verify

## PDF → JSON mapping

| PDF section | JSON path |
|-------------|-----------|
| Header (name, age, contacts, location) | `personal` |
| Фото | `personal.photoUrl` → `/resume/avatar.jpg` (file in `public/resume/`) |
| Желаемая должность | `personal.title` |
| Опыт работы (total) | `personal.totalExperience` |
| Гражданство / переезд / формат работы | `personal.citizenship`, `relocation`, `workFormats`, `employmentTypes` |
| Разрешение на работу | `personal.workPermit[]` — controls rabota.by button visibility (BY + RU) |
| Каждое место работы | `experience[]` — newest first |
| Строка "Стек - …" | `experience[].stack` (split by comma) |
| Bullet duties | `experience[].highlights` |
| Основной текст блока | `experience[].description` |
| Образование | `education[]` |
| Повышение квалификации | `courses[]` |
| Навыки | `skills[]` |
| Знание языков | `languages[]` |
| Опыт вождения | `driving` |
| Рекомендации | `recommendations` |
| Обо мне | `about` |

## Personal object — required fields

```json
{
  "name": "...",
  "title": "...",
  "location": "...",
  "citizenship": "...",
  "workPermit": ["Belarus", "Russia"],
  "relocation": "...",
  "totalExperience": "...",
  "employmentTypes": [],
  "workFormats": [],
  "contacts": {
    "phone": "...",
    "email": "...",
    "telegram": "...",
    "telegramUrl": "https://t.me/...",
    "portfolio": "https://..."
  },
  "pdfUrl": "/resume/FM-resume.pdf",
  "photoUrl": "/resume/avatar.jpg"
}
```

Use localized strings in each locale file (`Беларусь`/`Belarus`, etc.).

## Experience object template

```json
{
  "company": "Company name",
  "location": "City",
  "website": "https://optional.com/",
  "industry": "Industry · sub-industry",
  "role": "Job title",
  "period": "Month YYYY — Month YYYY",
  "duration": "N months",
  "description": "Main paragraph from PDF",
  "highlights": ["Bullet 1", "Bullet 2"],
  "stack": ["React", "TypeScript"]
}
```

## Rules

- Preserve text per locale (RU verbatim from PDF; EN as translation)
- Keep `experience` sorted newest → oldest (as in PDF)
- `personal.pdfUrl` must stay `/resume/FM-resume.pdf`
- `personal.photoUrl` must stay `/resume/avatar.jpg` unless photo path intentionally changes
- `meta.sourcePdf` must stay `/resume/FM-resume.pdf`
- Do not edit `CareerPage.tsx` or `generateResumePdf.ts` when only resume text/data changes
- After JSON update, no React code changes required unless schema changed
- Updating photo: replace `public/resume/avatar.jpg` (optionally sync from `src/assets/images/avatar.jpg`)
